§ `REQ-0284 (Haziq scenario h042) -- step 1, incorporating the private company`

-- s 19(1) falls on Haziq as promoter; s 19(2) on the RQI or a named director or secretary; s 146 on each named director before
-- incorporation; s 145 requires a resident director. On these facts the Registrar must register, and the company is private.
#ASSERT `the Registrar must register the constitution` `Haziq's private company`
#ASSERT `it may be incorporated as a private company` `Haziq's private company`
-- The sole director may not also be the secretary (s 171(1E)); the directors must appoint someone else (s 171(3)).
#ASSERT `section 171(1E) bars the candidate as secretary` 1 TRUE
-- Incorporated after the appointed day: the register of controllers is kept from the day of incorporation (s 386AF(1A)), and
-- Haziq at 55 of 75 shares (73.3%) is a registrable controller from the start.
#ASSERT `days after incorporation by which the register of controllers must be kept` TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `has a significant interest under paragraph 2` (`the percentage of the shares` 55 75) (`the percentage of the shares` 55 75)

§ `REQ-0284 -- step 2, issuing 25 shares to Ivan`

-- s 161: the directors need the prior approval of the company in general meeting; approval given on day 10, issue on day 40,
-- next AGM concluding day 300, AGM deadline day 365.
#ASSERT `the section 161 approval is in force on` 40 10 300 365 FALSE
#ASSERT `the issue is authorised under section 161` TRUE FALSE
-- Without approval the issue is void (s 161(6)).
#ASSERT `the issue is void under section 161(6)` (`the issue is authorised under section 161` FALSE FALSE)
-- s 63: a return of allotment, and the allotment takes effect only when the Registrar updates the register of members.
#ASSERT NOT `the private company's allotment has taken effect under section 63` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the private company's allotment has taken effect under section 63` FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Ivan holds exactly 25%.
#ASSERT `the percentage of the shares` 25 100 EQUALS 25
-- s 81 does not reach the company: Division 4 applies only to a Minister-declared body (s 79(2)).
#ASSERT NOT `has a substantial shareholding under section 81` FALSE 25
-- Were it declared, 25% would be a substantial shareholding, and the notice would be Ivan's, not the directors'.
#ASSERT `has a substantial shareholding under section 81` TRUE 25
#ASSERT `who must give the section 82 notice` EQUALS `the substantial shareholder`
-- Exactly 25% is not "more than 25%": Ivan is not a registrable controller by interest or by votes.
#ASSERT NOT `has a significant interest under paragraph 2` 25 25
#ASSERT NOT `the company must enter the person in its register of controllers` FALSE (`has significant control under paragraph 1` FALSE 25 FALSE) FALSE FALSE

§ `REQ-0284 -- step 3, buying back Bee's 20 shares`

#ASSERT `the selective off-market purchase is authorised` `buying back Bee's 20 shares with Ivan abstaining and consenting`
-- 20 of 100 is exactly the s 76B(3) ceiling, and within it.
#ASSERT `the acquisition is within the section 76B(3) limit` `buying back Bee's 20 shares with Ivan abstaining and consenting`
-- Ivan can block it: 55 for, 25 against is 68.75%, under three-fourths.
#ASSERT NOT `the special resolution passes in a private company` `the same buy-back with Ivan voting against`
#ASSERT NOT `the selective off-market purchase is authorised` `the same buy-back with Ivan voting against`
-- And again by withholding class consent under s 76D(2A): Haziq alone is 50% of the other holders.
#ASSERT NOT `the selective off-market purchase is authorised` `the same buy-back with only Haziq's class consent`
-- Lawful only if the company is solvent at the date of payment (s 76F).
#ASSERT `the buy-back is lawful` TRUE (`the company is solvent under section 76F(4)` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the buy-back is lawful` TRUE (`the company is solvent under section 76F(4)` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- 80 shares remain; Ivan's 25 are now 31.25%, over 25%: the company must now enter him in its register of controllers.
#ASSERT `shares in issue after the buy-back` 100 20 EQUALS 80
#ASSERT `the percentage of the shares` 25 80 EQUALS 31.25
#ASSERT `the company must enter the person in its register of controllers` (`has a significant interest under paragraph 2` 31.25 31.25) FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `REQ-0284 -- step 4, incorporating the company limited by guarantee`

#ASSERT `the Registrar must register the constitution` `Haziq's guarantee company`
-- No share capital, so it cannot be private: it is a public company (ss 17(5), 18(1), 4(1)).
#ASSERT NOT `it may be incorporated as a private company` `Haziq's guarantee company`
#ASSERT `it will be a public company` `Haziq's guarantee company`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must register the constitution` `the guarantee company with a share capital`

§ `Incorporation -- each requirement in turn`

#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must register the constitution` `the same company with no director resident in Singapore`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must register the constitution` `the same company whose director had not filed consent before incorporation`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must register the constitution` `the same company with no section 19(2) declaration by anyone the Act names`
-- Without a transfer restriction it is registered as a public company.
#ASSERT `it will be a public company` `the same company whose constitution does not restrict transfers`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must register the constitution` `the guarantee company whose constitution omits the guarantee`
#ASSERT `the secretary's office has been vacant too long` 7

§ `Section 157`

#ASSERT `the director is in breach of section 157(1)` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the maximum fine under section 157(3), in dollars` EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment under section 157(3), in months` EQUALS 12

§ `Section 161 -- the life of an approval`

-- Spent at the earlier of the next AGM's conclusion (day 300) and its deadline (day 365).
#ASSERT NOT `the section 161 approval is in force on` 300 10 300 365 FALSE
#ASSERT `the section 161 approval is in force on` 299 10 300 365 FALSE
-- s 161(4): an issue under an offer made while an approval authorising it was in force survives the approval's lapse.
#ASSERT `the issue is authorised under section 161` FALSE TRUE
-- s 161(7): two years to sue a director who knowingly issued without approval.
#ASSERT `proceedings lie against the director under section 161(7)` FALSE TRUE 24
#ASSERT NOT `proceedings lie against the director under section 161(7)` FALSE TRUE 25

§ `Division 4 -- when a body is declared`

#ASSERT `the section 83 percentage level` 31.25 EQUALS 31
#ASSERT `a section 83 notice is due` TRUE 25 31.25
#ASSERT `a section 84 notice is due` TRUE 5 4.9

§ `Part 11A -- controllers`

#ASSERT `has significant control under paragraph 1` FALSE 10 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the company must enter the person in its register of controllers` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `has a significant interest under paragraph 3` 0 26

§ `Buy-back -- each requirement in turn`

#ASSERT NOT `the selective off-market purchase is authorised` `the same buy-back with Bee voting her shares`
#ASSERT NOT `the selective off-market purchase is authorised` `the same buy-back without a permission in the constitution`
#ASSERT NOT `the acquisition is within the section 76B(3) limit` `buying back 21 of 100 shares`
#ASSERT `the acquisition is within the section 76B(3) limit` `buying back 21 of 100 shares after a section 78B reduction`
#ASSERT NOT `the special resolution passes in a private company` `the same buy-back on 13 days' notice`
#ASSERT NOT `the selective off-market purchase is authorised` `the same buy-back with the agreement open for 14 days`
#ASSERT `the selective off-market purchase is authorised` `the same buy-back by written resolution with no inspection`
-- s 76F(4)(b) forks on intention to wind up: paying in full within 12 months of the winding up suffices.
#ASSERT `the company is solvent under section 76F(4)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the director commits the section 76F(3) offence` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the maximum fine under section 76F(3), in dollars` EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT NOT `the private company's buy-back has taken effect` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `The company limited by guarantee`

-- Required 5,000, guarantee 100.
#ASSERT `the guarantee contribution` 5000 100 TRUE 0 TRUE EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the guarantee contribution` 5000 100 FALSE 12 TRUE EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the guarantee contribution` 5000 100 FALSE 13 TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the provision is void under section 38(1)` TRUE TRUE
